  title: Post-War Reforms (1950s-1965)
  info: After World War II, education became a tool for rebuilding Singapore. The
    government emphasized universal primary education and invested in teacher training.
    Schools began shifting focus toward practical subjects like science and mathematics
    to prepare students for industrialization.
